<% content_for :title, "ROI Calculator — whizwheel" %>

<%#
  ROI (return on investment) calculator page (spec issue #258, DESIGN.md BLEND). Given the
  amount invested and the amount returned, compute the total gain and the ROI %; with an
  optional investment period (years), also the annualized ROI (CAGR). Single-formula, multi-
  input (Percentage-shaped) — NO mode picker; the only branch is whether the optional period
  was supplied (which adds the annualized figure).

  The form posts over Turbo and re-renders the #result region in place; it works WITHOUT JS —
  the server validates and re-renders the result fragment. No field depends on another, so the
  Stimulus controller is pure polish: it previews the live total-gain/ROI sign (gain vs. loss
  tinting) as the user types, mirroring the server result's accent-green/coral treatment. The
  no-JS baseline is unchanged.

  Layout per DESIGN.md §3 — an input column + a results panel (≈380px 1fr), collapsing to one
  column on mobile. Spacing scale ("targets not minimums"):
    • money/percent affixes → gap-2 (Affix tier — the $/% next to its field)
    • stacked fields        → space-y-5
    • fields → submit (major blocks) → mt-8 (Section tier)
    • column gutters / card padding → gap-8 / p-7–p-8 (Layout tier)
%>

<header class="max-w-2xl">
  <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-accent">Financial</p>
  <h1 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.035em] text-ink">ROI Calculator</h1>
  <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
    Return on investment — enter what you put in and what you got back to see your total gain
    and ROI percentage. Add an optional holding period and we'll also compute the annualized
    return (the compound annual growth rate). Every answer is computed server-side.
  </p>
</header>

<div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[380px_1fr]">
  <%# ── Input column ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── %>
  <section class="rounded-[18px] border border-border bg-surface p-7 shadow-[0_10px_34px_rgba(150,110,80,0.12)] sm:p-8">
    <%= form_with url: "/calculators/roi", scope: :inputs, method: :post,
          data: { controller: "roi" } do |f| %>

      <%# Section eyebrow + a live direction-preview chip (JS-only sugar). The chip reads
          "Gain"/"Loss"/"Break-even" once both money fields hold a value, mirroring the server
          result's sign tint (DESIGN.md §1/§6 — word + colour, never colour alone). Hidden
          until JS connects and both fields are filled; the answer is always the server's. %>
      <div class="mb-5 flex items-center gap-2">
        <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-faint">Your investment</p>
        <span data-roi-target="preview" hidden
              class="ml-auto rounded-full bg-current/10 px-2.5 py-0.5 text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.08em] text-faint"></span>
      </div>

      <%# Fields. Money fields carry a leading $ affix, the period a trailing "years" unit
          (Affix tier — gap-2, the symbol next to its field, DESIGN.md §3). Stacked tier:
          space-y-5 down the column. %>
      <div class="space-y-5">
        <%# Amount invested — money, leading $ affix. %>
        <div>
          <%= f.label :amount_invested, "Amount invested", class: "field-label", for: "inputs_amount_invested" %>
          <div class="mt-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-sm font-bold text-label" aria-hidden="true">$</span>
            <%= f.number_field :amount_invested, id: "inputs_amount_invested", step: "any",
                  inputmode: "decimal", min: "0", placeholder: "0",
                  class: "field-input", data: { roi_target: "invested", action: "roi#preview" } %>
          </div>
        </div>

        <%# Amount returned — money, leading $ affix. %>
        <div>
          <%= f.label :amount_returned, "Amount returned", class: "field-label", for: "inputs_amount_returned" %>
          <div class="mt-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-sm font-bold text-label" aria-hidden="true">$</span>
            <%= f.number_field :amount_returned, id: "inputs_amount_returned", step: "any",
                  inputmode: "decimal", min: "0", placeholder: "0",
                  class: "field-input", data: { roi_target: "returned", action: "roi#preview" } %>
          </div>
        </div>

        <%# Investment period — OPTIONAL; supplying it unlocks the annualized ROI. A trailing
            "years" unit affix, and a one-line helper naming what it adds (so "optional" reads
            as a feature, not an omission). Blank stays blank — never auto-prefilled. %>
        <div>
          <%= f.label :investment_years, class: "field-label", for: "inputs_investment_years" do %>
            Investment period <span class="font-medium normal-case tracking-normal text-faint">(optional)</span>
          <% end %>
          <div class="mt-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
            <%= f.number_field :investment_years, id: "inputs_investment_years", step: "any",
                  inputmode: "decimal", min: "0", placeholder: "0",
                  class: "field-input" %>
            <span class="text-sm font-bold text-label" aria-hidden="true">years</span>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-1.5 text-[13px] leading-snug text-faint">
            Add a holding period to also get the annualized ROI.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <%# Submit — Section tier above; primary coral button (DESIGN.md §4). %>
      <%= f.submit "Calculate",
            class: "mt-8 w-full cursor-pointer rounded-[13px] bg-primary px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-surface shadow-sm transition-opacity hover:opacity-90 focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent" %>
    <% end %>
  </section>

  <%# ── Results panel (the Turbo target) ─────────────────────────────────── %>
  <section id="result" aria-live="polite">
    <%= render "calculators/result", calc: nil %>
  </section>
</div>
